.git
# Same trap as the data entry below: a bare "node_modules" only matches the context root, so every
# workspace package's node_modules was copied in from the developer's machine. pnpm fills those with
# symlinks into a store the image does not have, and the build died on "Cannot find module
# next/dist/bin/next" — after five days in which every local image build failed and the stack kept
# quietly serving the last one that worked.
**/node_modules
.next
coverage
# Matches at any depth. A bare "data" only excludes the context root, so a developer's
# apps/web/data/app/state.json was copied into locally built images while CI, building from a clean
# checkout where that gitignored directory does not exist, produced a different image. The app then
# loads it as legacy state on first boot.
**/data
# Long-lived dev stack state; contains container-owned files the build context cannot read.
.dev-stack
test-results
*.log

